## New Capabilities Identified

- **Dual-pane graph view**: an independent 1-pane/2-pane control, positioned beside the Options & help hamburger, orthogonal to the existing force-directed/swim-lane mode toggle. In 2-pane mode both layouts render side by side with synced node selection across both panes and the shared side panel. Available only above a wide-screen breakpoint (exact px value deferred to epic planning); below it, behaves exactly as today.
- **Theme chooser**: extends the existing Color theme section with 3 CVD-validated font+accent presets (chrome + graph-node-palette synced, same validation process as the shipped teal/Manrope refresh) plus a 4th "Custom" option (chrome-only, accessibility-unvalidated, disclosed in the UI). Persists via localStorage.

## Priority Signal

User explicitly prioritized these two capabilities ahead of the already-scoped-but-unimplemented Guided Tour epic (2Ze47tg) and Keyboard De-escalation epic (eMNbiFL) — both of which remain queued for after this cycle. Within this session: pane control must be a separate, always-visible control beside the hamburger (not folded into the existing mode toggle or the Options popover), and the theme chooser must include the custom-color option, not just 3 fixed presets — both were explicit, non-default choices over the recommended simpler alternatives presented during the interview.

## Deferred Items

- Whether dual-pane mode should ever be forceable below the wide-screen breakpoint — explicitly deferred in favor of the existing 390px-floor auto-fallback precedent.
- Guided Tour epic (2Ze47tg) and Keyboard De-escalation epic (eMNbiFL) — both already-scoped, un-implemented epics from a prior cycle, explicitly deferred behind this cycle's work per the user's stated priority.
